35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission trial worked, but only while it ran. The shared nursing round lost a third of visits.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The booking system only logs named slots. Ad-hoc work disappears. The car park fills by eleven.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The joint clinic closed in a year. Neither department held the budget. Data agreements take fourteen months.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Physiotherapists are leaving for the city. Midwifery has slack. Ward nursing is covered by expensive agency staff.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,The development budget is down a quarter. Home visits earn no tariff. Only on-site sessions bill.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if home visits earn nothing, how do we justify the cost? The trial data is promising, though.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, fourteen months for data agreements is a dealbreaker for anything relying on outside records.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, exactly. The joint clinic failed because the structure was fragile. We must avoid that trap.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, the midwifery slack is interesting. But the ward vacancies are a crisis.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, agency cover is eating the budget. We need a program that uses existing slack, not new hires.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission drop was significant. But the shared round failed due to logistics, not intent.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The booking system is a bottleneck. Any program needing flexible, unbooked time will vanish from reports.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The data agreement delay means we cannot easily link with outside surgeries. That limits coordination options.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"Midwifery has capacity. Therapy is draining. We should lean into the slack, not the shortage.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,The tariff structure favors on-site work. Home visits are a financial black hole unless subsidized.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
